I tricked cmake into showing me the gcc line it was calling to link cygnethack.dll (libnethack.dll.a). I added /usr/lib/libz.a to the end of that gcc line, and ran it, and it created cygnethack.dll.

Continuing with the build, I had to make sure the libncurses-devel package was installed from cygwin, and also libjansson (the JSON parser). libjansson is not known by the standard cygwin setup.exe, so I downloaded source from here
http://fd0.x0.to/cygwin/release/jansson/
and built it according to the package instructions.  (It *looked* like a cyg port but I wasn't sure how to make setup.exe use it.)

After that, no more issues. make succeeded, and so did make install. I have a working nethack 4 under Cygwin!

As soon as I figure out how to package the binary and all its dependencies, I'll put it up for download. Then I'll tackle making it compile statically, or with mingw gcc instead of cygwin gcc, or something.


